  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-81987\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>Let's recall the following facts:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement. </p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-81987-e-0\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-81987-e-0\"></div>\n\n<p>So, we are looking for the contrapositive.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Statement I is the contrapositive. <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"178\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 1em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mstyle style=\"color: green;\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2713 TEX-A\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace></mstyle><mstyle mathcolor=\"green\"><mi>✓</mi></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Statement II is the converse, not the contrapositive. <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"179\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 1em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mstyle style=\"color: red;\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-cD7\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace></mstyle><mstyle mathcolor=\"red\"><mo>×</mo></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Statement III is the inverse, not the contrapositive. <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"180\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mspace style=\"width: 1em;\"></mjx-mspace></mjx-mstyle><mjx-mstyle style=\"color: red;\"><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-cD7\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mstyle scriptlevel=\"0\"><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace></mstyle><mstyle mathcolor=\"red\"><mo>×</mo></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Therefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"</p>\n<div class=\"studentAnswerHeader\">Your Answer:</div><div class=\"studentAnswer\">II and III only</div></div>",
